# Keep the build context free of anything the image should not depend on.
#
# node_modules matters most: without this, a local `docker build` sweeps in the
# developer's installed tree, and the build can succeed for reasons that do not
# exist on a clean checkout. That happened — a local build passed only because
# it picked up a nested zod 3 from the host, while the NAS build failed, since
# its deploy directory only ever receives source. Excluding it here forces every
# build to depend solely on `npm ci` output, so local and remote agree.
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Never ship secrets or local state into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.claude
.git
.github

# Noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.vscode
**/.idea
